+## Cooldown identity and duration integrity
+
+October17 audit/candidate source2279169, draft PR219 stacked on Monk PR218:
+`C:/Users/verre/Documents/Codex/2026-10-17/see/work/cooldown-audit`.
+Duration fixes are implemented/tested, not deployed. Signed clamps prevent item,
+Mend and Bash/Frenzy reuse reductions becoming uint32 century-long lockouts.
+Linked spell completion decodes the signed focus in its uint32 millisecond wire
+field before division. Native PersistentTimer::Start(0) retains/restarts the old
+duration: zero AA/linked completion clears the timer; fully reduced Mend, Hide,
+Feign Death, Disarm/Sense Traps skip Start after the existing expiry gate.
+Normal reuse, negative focus, success/proc/trigger guards and ownership remain.
+GetFocusEffect returns int64; native UseDiscipline correctly handles negative
+focus already. Do not change it based on an inaccurate int32 test double.
+
+The read-only production catalog audit is separate from gameplay confirmation.
+17 raw AA groups span157 allowed ordinary activated families. Actual methods
+reproduce Divine Resurrection blocking Divine Stun for18h and Harm Touch/LoH
+sharing reuse. Harmshield/Cannibalize use linked group1; Battle Cry/Throw Stone
+use discipline8 with canonical current-level access. Unrelated group separation
+is still open; retain ranks and reviewed deliberate links. Client bounded spell/
+disc groups require paired readiness/reset/resend changes, not server-only keys.
+Existing ambiguous saved timers require a designed transition, never a blanket
+clear. The saved aggregate contained no multi-year timer; active zone memory and
+the reported player's exact incident were not observed. Current widened SQL
+spell classes are not ownership evidence; use spell_class_catalog.h.
+
+Source: zone/{spells,client_packet,special_attacks}.cpp. Tests:
+tools/tests/test_cooldown_duration.py (18 tests/28 scenarios, actual native
+lifecycle and full UseDiscipline), test_monk_combat_reuse.py (16 tests, preserving
+six-skill isolation plus Bash/Frenzy boundaries). Adjacent policy2, AA-duration19
+and spell-access2 pass. Independent code/evidence review passes. The release's
+reproduce_collisions.py deliberately remains six RED/five control cases; it is
+an audit diagnostic, not passing regression evidence. Full zone build is pending
+because local Docker's Linux engine is unavailable. Build current retained source;
+rule/quest reload is insufficient. No new wire/ItemData/schema change, but the
+inherited Monk work still requires proxy0.9.2-dev. No live repair or activation.
+Exact audit inventories, tests, pairing and QA: docs/releases/cooldown-audit-20261017/.
