+## Item recast timer integrity
+
+October17 cooldown candidate2279169 (PR219, not deployed) clamps signed click
+reuse reductions before uint32 conversion in zone/spells.cpp::SetItemRecastTimer.
+Excess reduction previously yielded roughly136 years. Actual-method tests cover
+ordinary/negative/equal/excess focus and augment packet suppression. Pair current
+zone build with the inherited Monk release requirements; this duration delta adds
+no item ABI/cache/schema/client layout change. Do not erase existing player timers.
+
+Identity remains an open defect: pTimerType is uint16, so unlinked -item_id keys
+alias at65536 intervals and can overlap spell timers. Read-only current content
+has1158 unlinked definitions, two item-pair groups and364 item cross-domain
+catalog aliases; reachability/ownership of individual examples is not proven.
+Native methods reproduce read, overwrite and delete collisions. The6640 named
+group definitions retain deliberate shared reuse. A fix needs stable disjoint
+positive domains and wider native keys compatible with SQL timers.type's24-bit
+unsigned range; widening negative keys to uint32 alone is invalid. Include every
+item/augment verify, set/get/delete, saved timestamp and client-refresh path.
+Audit, failure reproducer, source fingerprint and QA: docs/releases/cooldown-audit-20261017/ in the cooldown-audit checkout listed in multiclass.md.
